// Firestore Security Rules for mistamerica-job-tracker
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// APPLY THESE — the app is not protected until you do.
//
//   1. Firebase console → Authentication → Sign-in method → enable "Google".
//      (Required first, or sign-in in the app will fail.)
//   2. Open:
//      https://console.firebase.google.com/project/mistamerica-job-tracker/firestore/rules
//   3. Replace everything there with the rules below (from "rules_version").
//   4. Click PUBLISH.
//   5. In the app, tap "Sign in to sync" and pick your Google account.
//
// Do step 1 BEFORE step 4, or you'll lock yourself out until you finish.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// WHAT CHANGED AND WHY
//
// The previous rules scoped access to /users/lyle-mistamerica/** and then said
// `allow read, write: if true`. That path is hardcoded in index.html, which is
// served publicly from GitHub Pages — so anyone who viewed source could read the
// entire record, and could also ALTER OR DELETE it. For a file whose whole value
// is being an unaltered contemporaneous record, unauthenticated write access was
// the real problem.
//
// These rules require a signed-in Google account whose verified email matches
// OWNER_EMAIL. Everything else — every other path, every other account, every
// unauthenticated request — is denied.
//
// The data path is deliberately UNCHANGED. Existing records stay exactly where
// they are; nothing needs migrating.

rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {

    // The single owner of this record. Google verifies the email, and Firebase
    // signs the token, so this cannot be spoofed by editing client code.
    function isOwner() {
      return request.auth != null
          && request.auth.token.email_verified == true
          && request.auth.token.email == 'lylekrug@gmail.com';
    }

    // The app's data path. Same location as before — now owner-only.
    match /users/lyle-mistamerica/{collection}/{doc} {
      allow read, write: if isOwner();
    }

    // Everything else is denied, including probing for other collections.
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// IF YOU EVER CHANGE THE OWNER EMAIL
//
// Update the address in isOwner() above and re-publish. If you'd rather pin to
// a Firebase UID instead of an email (slightly stricter — survives an email
// change on the Google account), sign in once, then read your UID at:
//   Firebase console → Authentication → Users
// and swap the isOwner() body for:
//
//   return request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == '<YOUR-UID>';
//
// VERIFYING THE LOCK WORKED
//
// Open the app in a private/incognito window without signing in. The sync
// indicator should read "Sign in to sync" and no job data should load from the
// cloud. If data still appears, the rules did not publish — repeat step 3.
